      "writtenOn": "2022-06-20T23:33:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it makes more sense to clear the flag on any transition into G3 rather than treating S5 specially? We know any request to exit G3 is stale when we\u0027re entering G3 (because the AP was already on), so it seems simplest to clear the flag at that point.",
      "revId": "4b4de344f89a544cff1d379acf5f35698a9a6946",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4413f806_a7d6c2ae",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-20T23:41:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that the AP isn\u0027t entering G3, but is instead going into S5 and then the AP is started again - meanwhile the flag is set (and not cleared) and next time the AP is shutdown to G3, it starts immediately.\nAt some point we need to clear the flag, and this point seems to be the most common place where the AP is going out of some power-down state. We could possibly remove the clear in the G3 state and just have the one place, and that could be OK.",
      "parentUuid": "9fb1df33_137b7853",
      "revId": "4b4de344f89a544cff1d379acf5f35698a9a6946",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ece5ca9_5416ecf5",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-21T00:05:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t clearing the flag on that later G3 entry be fine as well? The issue with clearing it anywhere but on G3 entry is that it can be set again while the AP is still on.\n\nThis wouldn\u0027t close the hole, it just makes it smaller whereas clearing the flag on G3 entry actually closes it.",
      "parentUuid": "4413f806_a7d6c2ae",
      "revId": "4b4de344f89a544cff1d379acf5f35698a9a6946",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4ca55b66_eef54e01",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-21T00:16:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not so much clearing the flag in G3 that\u0027s the issue, it\u0027s the action to take the AP out of G3 that is the problem, since that is left over from the previous cycle (since it wasn\u0027t cleared then).\nAt that point, the AP should stay in G3.",
      "parentUuid": "1ece5ca9_5416ecf5",
      "revId": "4b4de344f89a544cff1d379acf5f35698a9a6946",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b06cf2d9_9b1a5447",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
